# REQUIRES: python-api
# The stack of the entry of a Python simulation does not grow with its steps
# of energy (#305), on the CPU in double and mixed precision
# (Inputs/python_stack.py). The row of the observed columns was allocated
# where it is written, in the loops over steps of an entry that never returns
# (D215), and taken again at every step of energy: 32 bytes a step for 4
# columns and 48 for 5. The depth of the stack at the boundary
# (`Simulation._stack_in_use`) is the same to the byte after 1, 9, and 17
# steps of energy taken as last steps of parts and after 8 and 16 more at
# the rows of a reporter, for programs without observed columns, with 4 and
# with 5, with tunables and their derivative, and under a barostat; and no
# allocation of the stack of the lowered module of each is outside the first
# block of its function.
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_stack.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU Double | FileCheck %s -DMODE="CPU Double"
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_stack.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU Mixed | FileCheck %s -DMODE="CPU Mixed"
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: no observed column: the stack of the entry at the boundary after 1 step of energy: {{[0-9]+}} bytes; after 8 and 16 more as last steps of parts +0 and +0 bytes, and after 8 and 16 more at the rows of a reporter +0 and +0 bytes (bound 0): True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: no observed column: the lowered module has 0 allocations of the stack outside the first block of a function: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: 4 observed columns: the stack of the entry at the boundary after 1 step of energy: {{[0-9]+}} bytes; after 8 and 16 more as last steps of parts +0 and +0 bytes, and after 8 and 16 more at the rows of a reporter +0 and +0 bytes (bound 0): True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: 4 observed columns: the lowered module has 0 allocations of the stack outside the first block of a function: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: 5 observed columns: the stack of the entry at the boundary after 1 step of energy: {{[0-9]+}} bytes; after 8 and 16 more as last steps of parts +0 and +0 bytes, and after 8 and 16 more at the rows of a reporter +0 and +0 bytes (bound 0): True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: 5 observed columns: the lowered module has 0 allocations of the stack outside the first block of a function: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: 2 observed columns, a tunable, and the derivative in the tunables: the stack of the entry at the boundary after 1 step of energy: {{[0-9]+}} bytes; after 8 and 16 more as last steps of parts +0 and +0 bytes, and after 8 and 16 more at the rows of a reporter +0 and +0 bytes (bound 0): True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: 2 observed columns, a tunable, and the derivative in the tunables: the lowered module has 0 allocations of the stack outside the first block of a function: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: 4 observed columns under a barostat, coupled every 5 steps: the stack of the entry at the boundary after 1 step of energy: {{[0-9]+}} bytes; after 8 and 16 more as last steps of parts +0 and +0 bytes, and after 8 and 16 more at the rows of a reporter +0 and +0 bytes (bound 0): True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: 4 observed columns under a barostat, coupled every 5 steps: the lowered module has 0 allocations of the stack outside the first block of a function: True
# CHECK: python stack passed
